        "original_id": "f80a6894-0439-53ba-aeaa-b78e02e581e5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Tionne Watkins, Park So-yeon, Lisa Lopes, Anita McLoud, Edmund \"Eddie Hustle\" Clement, Kandi Burruss, Lee Hwi-jae, Kim Sung-joo, Lee Hoon\n- Organizations: TLC, T-ara\n- Products: \"Girl Talk\", \"3D\"\n- Events: 4th APAN Star Awards\n- Places: Des Moines, Iowa, Wonju, Gangwon Province, Wonju Gymnasium\n\nFacts:\n- Tionne Watkins was born in Des Moines, Iowa.\n- Tionne Watkins rose to fame in the early 1990s as a member of TLC.\n- \"Girl Talk\" was written for TLC's fourth studio album \"3D\" in 2002 by Lisa Lopes, Tionne Watkins, Anita McLoud, Edmund \"Eddie Hustle\" Clement, and Kandi Burruss.\n- The 4th APAN Star Awards was held at Wonju Gymnasium in Wonju, Gangwon Province on November 28, 2015.\n- The 4th APAN Star Awards was hosted by Lee Hwi-jae, Kim Sung-joo, Lee Hoon, and T-ara's Park So-yeon.\n- Park So-yeon is best known as the former main vocalist and member of T-ara.",
